-- 0000_baseline.sql — canonical Planit schema baseline.
-- Represents every currently deployed Planit-owned schema object. A fresh
-- database built from this baseline reproduces production (minus intentionally
-- excluded external artifacts) WITHOUT replaying abandoned intermediate designs.
-- Generated by squashing migrations 004,006,007,008,009,010,011,012,014,015,016,017,
-- 021,022,023,024,025 to their current (production) state, PLUS the
-- assistant_proposals / assistant_proposal_ops schema (originally
-- 026_assistant_proposals.sql on feature/assistant-phase-a, already deployed to
-- production and verified byte-for-byte against the linked prod schema on
-- 2026-07-31). Those assistant tables are already-deployed state, so they are
-- folded into the baseline — not carried as a forward migration.
-- Obsolete intermediate schema (001,002,003,005,013,019,020) is dropped entirely;
-- historical one-time transforms are folded into final DDL (e.g. public_pace_scans.started_at).
-- External/non-Planit object gh_trigger_log is intentionally NOT created.
-- Seed rows (checkpoints, community, club) live in supabase/seed.sql.
-- The eight *_updated_at triggers absent from prod (communities, igc_events, igc_players,
-- igc_rounds, igc_tee_times, igc_pairings, igc_comments, public_pace_checkpoints) are
-- intentionally NOT recreated; their updated_at columns remain without auto-maintenance,
-- matching production. A forward migration may restore them separately.


